= Appendix H — Eight-Week Study Plan

+ *Week 1:* Personal health, hygiene and access barriers.
+ *Week 2:* Nutrients, food labels, hydration and safe food handling.
+ *Week 3:* Medicines, substance-use risks and respectful support.
+ *Week 4:* Water, sanitation, waste and environmental hazards.
+ *Week 5:* Infection agents, transmission, prevention and care.
+ *Week 6:* NCDs, risk factors and mental wellbeing.
+ *Week 7:* Scene safety, emergency help and first-aid limits.
+ *Week 8:* Family life, consent, reproductive health and mixed practice.

Complete the chapter drill each week, mark it and read every explanation. Revisit uncertain questions after a gap, then attempt the timed papers separately. Use the master bank to identify remaining weak topics. Consult current local guidance and qualified advice for real health decisions.
